   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><br><div>You can have finer control of jittering with the geom_jitter() function. <a href=\"http://docs.ggplot2.org/0.9.3.1/geom_jitter.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://docs.ggplot2.org/0.9.3.1/geom_jitter.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792371663425000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2LkJ-KZcQaTBXcJHH9Wz2q\">http://docs.ggplot2.org/0.9.3.1/geom_jitter.html</a></div><div><br>\r\n\r\n</div><div>That might be a solution.</div><div><br></div><div>Jeremy</div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On 26 November 2013 09:17, Joseph Voelkel <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">jgv...@rit.edu</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br>\r\n\r\n</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\">\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div lang=\"EN-US\" link=\"blue\" vlink=\"purple\">\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">It seems that there is over-jittering in the following example. Ideas?<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"># Read in abalone data<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">abalone&lt;-read.csv(url(&quot;<a href=\"http://archive.ics.uci.edu/ml/machine-learning-databases/abalone/abalone.data\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://archive.ics.uci.edu/ml/machine-learning-databases/abalone/abalone.data&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792371663425000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2MiWhsJv8UadmOR8yEOf40\">http://archive.ics.uci.edu/ml/machine-learning-databases/abalone/abalone.data</a>&quot;),<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">                header=FALSE)<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">names(abalone)&lt;-c(&quot;Sex&quot;, &quot;Length&quot;, &quot;Diameter&quot;, &quot;Height&quot;, <u></u>\r\n<u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">                &quot;WholeWgt&quot;, &quot;ShuckedWgt&quot;, &quot;VisceraWgt&quot;, &quot;ShellWgt&quot;, &quot;Rings&quot;)<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">str(abalone)<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"># find ranges<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">range(abalone$Diameter) # note this range in particular<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">range(abalone$Rings)<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"># make 3 graphs<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">windows(4,4)<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">qplot(Diameter, Rings, data=abalone)<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">                # all seems fine<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">windows(4,4)<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">qplot(Diameter, Rings, data=abalone, position=&quot;jitter&quot;)<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">                # Rings: seems fine<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">                # But Diameter is over-jittered<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"># swap x,y<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">windows(4,4)<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">qplot(Rings,Diameter, data=abalone, position=&quot;jitter&quot;)<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">                # Both Rings and Diameter seem fine<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Joe<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Joseph G. Voelkel, Ph.D.<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Professor, Center for Quality and Applied Statistics<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Hugh Carey Bldg, 14-2530<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Kate Gleason College of Engineering<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Rochester Institute of Technology<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">V <a href=\"tel:585-475-2231\" value=\"+15854752231\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\">585-475-2231</a><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">F <a href=\"tel:585-475-5959\" value=\"+15854755959\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\">585-475-5959</a><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">joseph....@rit.edu</a><span><font color=\"#888888\"><u></u><u></u></font></span></p><span><font color=\"#888888\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n</font></span></div><span><font color=\"#888888\">\r\n</font></span></div></blockquote></div></div