  {
   "id": "tqH3kgWdqWMJ",
   "from": "Roman Luštrik",
   "author": "bfc2eb6b71169017",
   "date": "2013-11-26T17:46:39Z",
   "subject": "Re: Over-jittering?",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Have you tried controlling for the &quot;width&quot; and &quot;height&quot; of jitter? I would also recommend you add some transparency to your plot to show the more dense group in the middle. Something along the lines of <div>\r\n\r\n<br></div><div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">ggplot(abalone, aes(x = Diameter, y = Rings)) +</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">  theme_bw() +</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">  geom_jitter(position = position_jitter(width = 0.1, height = 0.25), alpha = 0.25)</font></div>\r\n\r\n</div><div><br></div><div>Cheers,</div><div>Roman</div><div><br></div><div><br></div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Tue, Nov 26, 2013 at 6:17 PM, Joseph Voelkel <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">jgv...@rit.edu</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br>\r\n\r\n</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\">\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div lang=\"EN-US\" link=\"blue\" vlink=\"purple\">\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">It seems that there is over-jittering in the following example. Ideas?<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"># Read in abalone data<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">abalone&lt;-read.csv(url(&quot;<a href=\"http://archive.ics.uci.edu/ml/machine-learning-databases/abalone/abalone.data\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://archive.ics.uci.edu/ml/machine-learning-databases/abalone/abalone.data&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792371663423000&amp;usg=AOvVaw37AyVT5zVOHMPA0Qd3rKjH\">http://archive.ics.uci.edu/ml/machine-learning-databases/abalone/abalone.data</a>&quot;),<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">                header=FALSE)<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">names(abalone)&lt;-c(&quot;Sex&quot;, &quot;Length&quot;, &quot;Diameter&quot;, &quot;Height&quot;, <u></u>\r\n<u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">                &quot;WholeWgt&quot;, &quot;ShuckedWgt&quot;, &quot;VisceraWgt&quot;, &quot;ShellWgt&quot;, &quot;Rings&quot;)<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">str(abalone)<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"># find ranges<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">range(abalone$Diameter) # note this range in particular<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">range(abalone$Rings)<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"># make 3 graphs<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">windows(4,4)<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">qplot(Diameter, Rings, data=abalone)<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">         